{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1765017,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Paper Presentation","festival_id":null,"organization_id":136795,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-02T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-11-04T17:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/paper-presentation-kamala-nehru-college-knc-du-delhi-1765017","region":"hybrid","details":"<p>What if the global economy was a game of strategy?<\/p>\n<p>Trade routes are changing, energy is becoming a tool of power, alliances are being redrawn, and emerging economies are demanding a bigger voice.<\/p>\n<p>And somewhere in the middle of all this is India.<\/p>\n<p>At ECOPHORIA - Paper Presentation Competition, participants are invited to pick their perspective on the changing global economic order and build an argument around it &mdash; with research, data and their own perspective.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Theme:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The global economic order is undergoing a profound transformation, with shifting alliances, trade routes, and centres of economic power.<\/li>\n<li>Amid these changes, India stands at a critical crossroads, balancing economic growth with geopolitical interests.<\/li>\n<li>The theme explores India's evolving role in global trade, energy, BRICS, and the Global South.It invites participants to analyse how India can navigate power, interdependence, and emerging economic opportunities in a rapidly changing world.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;Sub-Themes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>India and the Global Oil Market<\/li>\n<li>India and BRICS<\/li>\n<li>India and the Global South<\/li>\n<li>Other topics connected to the central theme, with a clear economic perspective<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Guidelines<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Round 1: Submit an abstract by 14 October.<\/li>\n<li>Round 2: Submit the full paper by 24 October.<\/li>\n<li>Round 3: Shortlisted teams will present their research and arguments on 4 November.<\/li>\n<li>Abstracts should demonstrate relevance to the theme, originality, economic referencing, and structured writing.<\/li>\n<li>Teams advancing to the second round must submit the paper within the given deadline.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Document Submission:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">File type: PDF<\/li>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">File Name Format: TeamName_CollegeName.pdf<\/li>\n<li aria-level=\"1\">Submission Mode: Through Unstop platform<\/li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Font Style &amp; Size:<\/strong> Use <em>Times New Roman<\/em>, font size <strong>12<\/strong> throughout the manuscript.<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Line Spacing:<\/strong> Maintain <strong>1.5 line spacing<\/strong> with justified alignment.<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Originality:<\/strong> The submission must be <strong>original, unpublished<\/strong>, and free from plagiarism.<\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li aria-level=\"1\"><strong>Submission Integrity:<\/strong> Papers found violating authorship, originality, or citation norms may be subject to rejection.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Regulations:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team size: 1&ndash;3 members.<\/li>\n<li>Team members may belong to different DU colleges and courses.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must keep their submission relevant to the stated theme.<\/li>\n<li>The paper should be research-based, supported by relevant data\/evidence, and present the team's own perspective.<\/li>\n<li>The final presentation should communicate the research clearly and allow the team to defend its arguments during questions.<\/li>\n<li>The final outcome will be decided on the basis of the paper and final presentation together.<\/li>\n<li>The decision of the judges and organizing committee will be final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Plagiarized or AI-generated content beyond acceptable limits will lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":